### Per-Frame Cost Breakdown (steady-state)

| Component | ms/frame | % of per-frame |
|-----------|----------|----------------|
| Blending (face parse + composite) | 49.7 | 80.5% |
| VAE decode | 8.5 | 13.8% |
| UNet forward | 3.6 | 5.8% |
| **Total per-frame** | **61.8** | |

**Key finding:** Blending dominates per-frame cost at 80.5%. The UNet (the usual suspect
in diffusion pipelines) is only 5.8% of per-frame cost. This confirms the Taiboli fork
analysis — the render path (UNet) is not the bottleneck.

